# Applies to estate-sentry-api/Dockerfile only (BuildKit reads
# <Dockerfile>.dockerignore beside it), whose context is the repository root:
# the API depends on ../estate-sentry-perception, and a context cannot reach
# outside itself.
#
# An allowlist, because a root context otherwise sends everything — including
# estate-sentry-perception/.venv, which carries torch and runs to gigabytes, and
# data/, which holds live database files. Admit nothing, then only the two
# projects the image is built from.
*
!estate-sentry-api
!estate-sentry-perception

# ...and nothing generated inside them.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.so
**/*.egg-info
**/dist
**/build
**/.uv_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov
**/.tox

# Django: a dev database or collected static from the host must never end up in
# the image — collectstatic runs at build time.
estate-sentry-api/db.sqlite3
estate-sentry-api/db.sqlite3-journal
estate-sentry-api/staticfiles
estate-sentry-api/media
**/*.log

# Secrets and local environment.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/*.env

# Editors and OS.
**/.vscode
**/.idea
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/.DS_Store
**/*.backup.*
